*.dll
*.exe
*.pdb
# C# OUTPUT, not a fixture: written by `Scvx.Console --loop` for plot_compare.py.
# Regenerated by any run, so committing it just churns the diff.
PoweredGuidance/scvx/python_ref/loop_cs.csv

## IDE
**/Properties/launchSettings.json
# NOT ignored, deliberately, unlike PoweredGuidance/gfold/python_ref/*.csv above:
# PoweredGuidance/scvx/python_ref/dyn_ref.csv, sub_ref.csv and loop_ref.csv are small
# FIXTURES, not outputs — they are the JAX/CVXPY oracles the C# checks diff
# against. Committing them means `Scvx.Console --verbose`, `--sub-scs`, `--loop`
# and `--rh` run standalone; regenerating them needs JAX + cvxpy, which is a
# heavy dependency to force on anyone who just wants to run the tests.
# loop_ref.csv also carries the `# consts` line the drift guard asserts against.

